From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikael Hug <mikaelhug@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:14:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8112-j473: put the speaker amplifier back
 in the sound card

Commit 24c6498c237f ("arm64: dts: apple: t8112-j473: leave the speaker
amplifier out of the sound card") kept the SN012776 off because the
image shipped no speaker protection. Debian 13 now provides that stack:
speakersafetyd 1.1.2 with apple/j473.conf, asahi-audio with the j473 DSP
graph and alsa-ucm-conf-asahi with "Mac mini J473", and the Bande image
installs it.

The kernel keeps the speaker safe without that daemon, as on Asahi:
macaudio limits "Speaker Volume" to the lowest step (about -100 dB) until
a process holds the "Speaker Volume Unlock" control and writes the magic
value at least every 250 ms, and it fails probe if it cannot apply the
amp gain, HPF and OCE settings. speakersafetyd is started by udev only
when the speaker sense PCM (pcmC0D2c, TAS2764 ISENSE/VSENSE on slots 0
and 2) exists, so the node and link have to be present for the
protection to run at all.

This restores the Asahi description of the j473 speaker unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UqitcmCNS6G33aQUShi39x
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8112-j473.dts | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8112-j473.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8112-j473.dts
index be08b47..89608bd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8112-j473.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8112-j473.dts
@@ -170,7 +170,6 @@ speaker_amp: codec@38 {
 		interrupts = <11 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
 		ti,imon-slot-no = <0>;
 		ti,vmon-slot-no = <2>;
-		status = "disabled";
 	};
 
 	jack_codec: codec@4b {
@@ -190,6 +189,17 @@ sound {
 		compatible = "apple,j473-macaudio", "apple,macaudio";
 		model = "Mac mini J473";
 
+		dai-link@0 {
+			link-name = "Speaker";
+
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&mca 0>;
+			};
+			codec {
+				sound-dai = <&speaker_amp>;
+			};
+		};
+
 		dai-link@1 {
 			link-name = "Headphone Jack";
 
